<div class="page-break"></div>
<h2>ABSTRACT</h2>
<p><strong>MEDIBRIDGE</strong> is an advanced, production-ready multilingual telemedicine and clinical tele-consultation platform developed as a modern single-page web application using React 18, Node.js, Express, Socket.IO, WebRTC, and MongoDB. The platform bridges geographical, operational, and linguistic divides in modern healthcare delivery by facilitating seamless, high-definition audio-video medical consultations between patients and healthcare practitioners across diverse linguistic backgrounds, backed by continuous live bidirectional speech-to-speech translation and certified on-demand human medical interpreter escalation.</p>
<p>The project addresses four pervasive challenges in contemporary healthcare delivery: severe clinical language barriers between rural patients and urban specialist doctors, high appointment scheduling friction with double-booking conflicts, fragmented post-consultation digital prescription workflows, and the total lack of certified real-time human interpreter integration in standard video conferencing tools. To resolve these challenges, MEDIBRIDGE implements a zero-latency WebRTC mesh capable of orchestrating both two-way doctor-patient consultations and three-way doctor-patient-interpreter triage rooms with low-latency browser media acquisition. Parallel to the audio stream, an ultra-fast multi-tier clinical translation pipeline (sub-200ms response time) captures continuous doctor-patient dialogues, applies phonetic normalization for transliterated speech, maps clinical terminology through a specialized medical lexicon, and refines machine translation outputs through a culturally respectful Tamil/Hindi/Telugu/Malayalam/Kannada honorific post-processing filter.</p>
<p>The system enforces strict role-based access control (RBAC) across four dedicated stakeholder domains: Patients, Doctors, Certified Medical Interpreters, and System Administrators. Appointment reservations are verified using transactional conflict-prevention algorithms, and doctors author structured, verifiable digital prescriptions complete with dosage frequencies, durations, and dietary advisories. All core modules were rigorously evaluated through 24 end-to-end unit, integration, and security test cases covering WebRTC signalling handshakes, continuous speech streaming, acoustic feedback suppression, multilingual lexicon mapping, and role-based route guards. The entire test suite completed with a 100% pass rate, validating MEDIBRIDGE as a clinically reliable, scalable, and equitable digital health solution.</p>
<p><strong>Keywords:</strong> Telemedicine, WebRTC, Multilingual Translation, Speech Recognition, Real-Time Signalling, Medical Interpreter, Role-Based Access Control, Digital Prescription, MongoDB, React.</p>
