<h3>1.4 Scope of the Project</h3>
<h4>Within Project Scope</h4>
<ul><li>Full end-to-end registration, authentication, and profile onboarding for Patients, Doctors, Interpreters, and Administrators.</li></ul>
<ul><li>Search and discovery portal with multi-parameter filtering (Medical Speciality, Spoken Languages, Consultation Mode, Location, Consultation Fee).</li></ul>
<ul><li>Interactive calendar booking with automatic time-slot generation and instant conflict rejection.</li></ul>
<ul><li>WebRTC browser media acquisition, camera/mic toggle, audio unblocking policy management, and connection resilience.</li></ul>
<ul><li>Continuous speech-to-text recognition, multi-tier neural translation fallback, and Tamil clinical honorific polishing.</li></ul>
<ul><li>Real-time in-call Language Bridge side panel featuring categorized Quick Phrases, manual text translation, and TTS voice readout.</li></ul>
<ul><li>Real-time socket dispatch system alerting active certified interpreters with room parameters and patient language pairs.</li></ul>
<ul><li>Complete digital prescription authoring, historical consultation logging, and patient medical record viewing.</li></ul>
<ul><li>Administrative control panel with user suspension/activation, doctor credential verification, and platform usage analytics.</li></ul>
<h4>Outside Project Scope (Future Releases)</h4>
<ul><li>Integration with physical hospital Electronic Health Record (EHR) hardware systems via HL7/FHIR protocols.</li></ul>
<ul><li>End-to-end commercial payment gateway checkout (UPI and cash/card receipts are simulated via database transaction logs).</li></ul>
<ul><li>Certified clinical liability indemnification (the platform provides diagnostic decision-support tools and disclaimer banners).</li></ul>
