<h1>CHAPTER 4</h1>
<h1>IMPLEMENTATION</h1>
<h3>4.1 Implementation Details &amp; Development Approach</h3>
<p>MEDIBRIDGE was implemented using an agile, modular architecture that enforces separation of concerns across presentation, state, real-time networking, business logic, and database persistence. The codebase is organized cleanly into <code>frontend/</code> and <code>backend/</code> directories.</p>
<p>The frontend is constructed with <strong>React 18</strong> and bundled with <strong>Vite 5</strong>. Application state is distributed cleanly across dedicated React Context providers:</p>
<ul><li><code>AuthContext.jsx</code>: Manages logged-in user state, profile data, JWT persistence in <code>localStorage</code>, and logout cleanup.</li></ul>
<ul><li><code>SocketContext.jsx</code>: Maintains a single persistent Socket.IO client connection initialized with auto-reconnection parameters.</li></ul>
<ul><li><code>ToastContext.jsx</code>: Surfaces non-blocking clinical alerts, toast notifications, and connection state banners.</li></ul>
<p>Routing is managed via <strong>React Router v6</strong>, with custom route wrappers:</p>
<ul><li><code>ProtectedRoute</code>: Enforces active session validation, redirecting unauthenticated traffic to <code>/login</code>.</li></ul>
<ul><li><code>AdminRoute</code>: Validates that the active session holds the <code>admin</code> role before granting access to <code>/admin</code>.</li></ul>
