<div class="page-break"></div>
<h3>5.3 Results and Discussion</h3>
<p>All 24 test cases completed with a 100% pass rate. </p>
<ul><li><strong>Clinical Precision &amp; Cultural Honorifics:</strong> Machine translation from English to Tamil often produces informal singular phrasing (e.g., "நீ", "உனக்கு", "சாப்பிடு"), which sounds rude in a medical consultation. The custom Unicode honorific polisher successfully transformed these occurrences into polite, culturally appropriate phrasing ("நீங்கள்", "உங்களுக்கு", "சாப்பிடுங்கள்") without introducing syntax distortions.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>Translation Speed &amp; Fallback Resilience:</strong> The multi-tier translation pipeline delivered translation results in under 180ms across common doctor-patient inquiries, well within conversational response tolerances.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>Acoustic Feedback Handling:</strong> In cross-device tests (laptop patient speaking to mobile doctor), the laptop mic occasionally picked up English audio from the laptop speaker. The intelligent speaker resolution engine correctly detected the English language and attributed it to the doctor, preventing speech attribution errors.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>Real-Time Appointment Synchronization:</strong> Socket notifications delivered newly booked appointments to the doctor dashboard immediately, eliminating the need for manual page refreshes.</li></ul>
<br/>
<div class="page-break"></div>
<div class="page-break"></div>
<h1>CHAPTER 6</h1>
<h1>CONCLUSION AND FUTURE ENHANCEMENT</h1>
<h3>6.1 Conclusion</h3>
<p>The <strong>MEDIBRIDGE</strong> project demonstrates that modern web standards (WebRTC, WebSocket, React 18, and Node.js) can be combined to build an accessible, secure, and culturally respectful telemedicine platform that overcomes language barriers in healthcare delivery. </p>
<p>By unifying doctor discovery, conflict-free appointment booking, browser-native video consultations, real-time speech translation with cultural honorific polishing, on-demand human interpreter escalation, and structured digital prescription generation, MEDIBRIDGE provides an end-to-end clinical workflow tailored for multilingual societies.</p>
<div class="page-break"></div>
<h3>6.2 Achievements</h3>
<ul><li><strong>Engineered a Zero-Plugin WebRTC Consultation Mesh:</strong> Implemented browser-native video consultations supporting two-way and three-way mesh calls without third-party meeting dependencies.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>Developed Multi-Tier Real-Time Translation Pipeline:</strong> Achieved conversational translation speeds (&lt; 200ms) with four fallback tiers and a specialized clinical lexicon.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>Built a Custom Cultural Honorific Refinement Engine:</strong> Ensured all translated medical interactions use respectful language.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>Implemented On-Demand Interpreter Escalation:</strong> Built a dispatch system that alerts online certified interpreters and integrates them into active calls.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>Eliminated Scheduling Conflicts:</strong> Built transactional queries that prevent double-booking for practitioners.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>Delivered Comprehensive Digital Prescriptions:</strong> Built structured prescription workflows with dosage, frequency, duration, and follow-up tracking.</li></ul>
<div class="page-break"></div>
<h3>6.3 Limitations</h3>
<ul><li><strong>Acoustic Speaker Echo in Speakerphone Mode:</strong> When testing without headphones in close proximity, microphone pick-up of speaker output can occasionally trigger double transcription.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>Mobile Self-Signed SSL Restrictions:</strong> Mobile Chrome on Android requires manual acceptance of local self-signed certificates before Web Speech APIs are enabled on private IP addresses.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>Dialectal Variation:</strong> While standard Tamil, Hindi, Telugu, Malayalam, and Kannada are supported, heavy regional idioms require continuous lexicon expansion.</li></ul>
<div class="page-break"></div>
<h3>6.4 What We Learned</h3>
<ul><li><strong>WebRTC State Machine Complexity:</strong> Managing asynchronous peer connections, ICE candidates, and track renegotiation across multiple peers requires clean cleanup logic.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>Unicode Text Processing in Non-Latin Scripts:</strong> Standard regex word boundaries (<code>\b</code>) fail on non-ASCII scripts. Using Unicode-aware boundary lookarounds (<code>\u0B80-\u0BFF</code>) is essential for reliable Tamil text processing.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>Resilient Audio/Video Strategies:</strong> Implementing automatic fallback canvas streams ensures video calls can be initiated even when hardware cameras are restricted.</li></ul>
<div class="page-break"></div>
<h3>6.5 Future Enhancements &amp; Roadmap</h3>
<p>The planned evolution of the MEDIBRIDGE platform is organized into six engineering phases in Table 6.1.</p>
